{"Asymmetric cache-first logic between Check and List methods: Check has fallthrough-to-DB logic when cached permissions don't grant access, but List uses cached permissions directly without any fallthrough-on-incomplete logic. If the permission cache is stale and missing recently granted permissions, List will silently return an incomplete result set while Check would self-correct by falling through to the DB. This creates inconsistency where a user may be granted access via Check (DB fallthrough) but the same resource is missing from List (stale cache).": 0.8813181519508362}